https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lrKVuKCD7Qo  (Capo 0) (MC0)

TIP:  Neil has the 6th string tuned down to <d> in order to get that low <d> first note in the intro.  If you elect to tune down then you’ll need to miss the 6th string on all the strums of (G).  If you prefer to stay in standard tuning then play the middle <d> which is the open 4th string.

TIP:  Individual notes may or may not transpose.  

TIP:  The whole (D) (Dsus2) (D) (Dsus2) sequence is easy to play as all you’re doing is lifting off the 1st string to get from (D) to (Dsus2) and replacing it again to get back to (D).

TIP:  For the (D) - (Bm) in the instrumental bridge hold the (D) and add your pinky to the 3rd string/4th fret and then remove it to get back to (D).


